  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.0 stable release\n\t\t\tAdds the virtual OnCancelAuthorityEpoch() hook so derived providers can\n\t\t\thandle cancellation-specific behavior at the actual cancellation point,\n\t\t\twithout depending on FinalDispose.\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tAdds HasEverRequestedAuthority(...) to report participation history\n\t\t\tseparately from authority currently held. This affects only custom\n\t\t\tIAuthorityEpochProvider implementations. The provided concrete\n\t\t\timplementation supports this automatically and serves as a guide for\n\t\t\tequivalent epoch-history tracking.\n\n\t\t\t1.0.3\n\t\t\tAdds TestableEpoch support for deterministic Guid and DateTimeOffset\n\t\t\tgeneration in unit tests, along with documentation and broader MSTest\n\t\t\tcoverage for repeatable fixture generation.\n\n\t\t\t1.0.2\n\t\t\tImproves usability by adding the default\n\t\t\tCancelAuthorityEpoch(@throw = false) behavior and promoting generic\n\t\t\tAuthority and Authorities members for easier direct consumption.\n\n\t\t\t1.0.1\n\t\t\tStrengthens the generic API with runtime type enforcement and expanded\n\t\t\ttest coverage for cancellation, mixed-authority scenarios, lifecycle\n\t\t\tinvariants, awaitable completion, and context snapshot behavior.\n\n\t\t\t1.0.0\n\t\t\tInitial release of AuthorityEpochProvider for authority-based coordination\n\t\t\tover DisposableHost epochs, including first-wins authority selection,\n\t\t\treference-counted participation, and deterministic FinalDispose behavior.",
